# Audio stack: native Web Audio, libraries as ingredients only

Full reasoning: `docs/audio-stack.md`. Feel rules: `AGENTS.md` §5.

## Do not install an audio framework

No `tone`, `@elemaudio/*`, `howler`, `pizzicato`, or anything that owns the
`AudioContext`, the clock, or "now". Instrumaps runs on **one** shared
context (`AudioContextProvider`) and **one** clock (`useLessonClock`) that
drives both sound and visuals. A framework that owns time becomes
load-bearing in the UI. Data-only packages (`@tonejs/midi` for parsing) are
fine — they never touch the audio thread.

## Adoption rule — a sound dependency needs all three

1. Native nodes genuinely cannot make the sound (custom DSP via
   `AudioWorklet`), not "saves typing".
2. It sits behind our interface: `src/lib/audio/voices/*.ts` or `Effect`
   signatures do not change if the inside is swapped.
3. MIT / BSD / LGPL-compatible, and it is an **algorithm**, not a framework.

"It would be faster with Tone" is never a reason. Revisit per component,
never wholesale.

## Six guardrails every sound file follows

| Never | Always |
|---|---|
| `new AudioContext()` in a component | `useSharedAudioContext()`; `resume()` inside the gesture handler |
| schedule from `setTimeout` / render | absolute `when` from `AudioContext.currentTime` via the shared clock |
| start a source without an end | `stop(t)` + `onended` cleanup; envelopes reach 0 before stop |
| connect straight to `destination` | through `createLessonBus()` (gain → lowpass → reverb → compressor limiter) |
| unbounded voices | cap ~32, steal oldest |
| React state per step / per hit | refs + `requestAnimationFrame`; state only for what the user sees change |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — private context, timer scheduling, no end, straight out
const ctx = new AudioContext();
setTimeout(() => { const o = ctx.createOscillator(); o.connect(ctx.destination); o.start(); }, 500);

// ✅ GOOD — shared context, absolute time, bounded, on the bus
kickAt(ctx, bus, when, velocity);  // src/lib/audio/voices/drums.ts builds, envelopes, stops
```

## Where sound code lives

- `src/lib/audio/` — UI-free recipes: `bus.ts`, `noise.ts`, `voices/*.ts`.
  Pure functions taking `(ctx, bus, …, when)`; checkable from `/tmp`.
- React bindings (`ProgressionProvider`, `useDrumKit`) call the recipes;
  they do not build node graphs themselves.
- Music theory stays in `src/lib/music/`; it names voices, never makes them.

## Samples

Synthesis first (`AGENTS.md` §5). If a voice tops out after tuning by ear,
an openly-licensed one-shot may drop in behind the **same** function
signature, credited, under `public/audio/`. Per voice, noted in the file
header — never a wholesale switch.
